From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:16:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] web-app: type-check fork strings from
 packages/web-app/fork-strings.json

The fork's English strings live in packages/web-app/fork-strings.json,
which assemble.mjs merges into dist/locales/_untranslated_en.json, not in
_locales/_untranslated_en.json. TranslationKey is built from the locale
files, so without this every tx('<fork key>') call is a type error
(50 of them in check:types). Importing the fork file's keys as well
keeps the type strict: an unknown key still fails.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 packages/shared/translationKeyType.d.ts | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/shared/translationKeyType.d.ts b/packages/shared/translationKeyType.d.ts
index 8496babc7c0654e1c833e80fbf8f31fbc5bbb0d2..edf4acf2b3a783ec1ac3ae656acf620b38a4a9ee 100644
--- a/packages/shared/translationKeyType.d.ts
+++ b/packages/shared/translationKeyType.d.ts
@@ -2,9 +2,13 @@
 import type english from '../../_locales/en.json'
 //@ts-ignore
 import type untranslated from '../../_locales/_untranslated_en.json'
+// slothfulchat-web: the fork's strings live outside this tree and are merged
+// into _untranslated_en.json when dist/ is assembled.
+//@ts-ignore
+import type fork from '../../../../packages/web-app/fork-strings.json'
 
 //@ts-ignore
-export type TranslationKey = keyof typeof english | keyof typeof untranslated
+export type TranslationKey = keyof typeof english | keyof typeof untranslated | keyof typeof fork
 
 // The ignore here is to make it optional,
 // if the import fails (because resolveJsonModule=false) it should bring down everything with it.
